E('hostile','英 /ˈhɒstaɪl/；美常 /ˈhɑːstəl/，也读 /ˈhɑːstaɪl/','敌对的；不友好的；不利生存的','感觉对面正在排斥你，或环境根本不给你顺利待下去的条件。','来自法语 hostile 或拉丁 hostilis，接 hostis“敌人”；不要拆成英语 host“主人” + 一个虚构词尾。',HOSTILE,'hostile to a proposal 是反对提案；a hostile crowd 带敌意；a hostile environment 可能是极寒、缺氧等严酷环境。hostile takeover 则指被收购方管理层不支持的收购。','hostile to；a hostile reception；a hostile environment。','unfriendly 可只是冷淡；hostile 常更强，含排斥、对抗或伤害性条件。',('The audience was openly hostile to his proposal.','听众公开反对他的提案。'),('Few plants can survive in such a hostile environment.','很少有植物能在这么严酷的环境里生存。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/hostile','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/hostile']),
E('hostility','英 /hɒˈstɪləti/；美 /hɑːˈstɪləti/','敌意；强烈反对；敌对行为','不只是意见不同，而是对方把你当成需要抵抗、排斥的对象。','经古法语 hostilité 或晚期拉丁 hostilitas 借入；名词在英语中较早出现，历史不能仅写成 hostile + -ity。',HOSTILITY,'通常不可数，show hostility to/towards somebody 是表现敌意。公共讨论中的 hostility to change 是强烈抗拒改变；不一定已经动武。','open hostility；hostility towards；meet with hostility。','disagreement 是意见不合；hostility 还带对人的敌意或强烈对抗。',('Her suggestion met with unexpected hostility.','她的建议遭到了出乎意料的强烈反对。'),('There was no sign of hostility between the neighbours.','邻居之间看不出有什么敌意。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/hostility','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/hostility']),
E('hostilities','英 /hɒˈstɪlətiz/；美 /hɑːˈstɪlətiz/','交战；敌对行动〔通常复数〕','敌意已经变成实际冲突：不是心里不喜欢，而是双方在打、在对抗。','hostility 的复数，y 改为 -ies；复数逐渐固定用于交战、战争行动。',HOSTILITY+[['英语 hostility → hostilities','敌对行为 → 交战、战事']],'the outbreak of hostilities 是战事爆发；cease hostilities 是停止敌对行动。复数也可用于较小规模冲突，但新闻、外交中常带军事含义。','cease hostilities；renewed hostilities；the outbreak of hostilities。','hostility 可是态度；hostilities 通常指已经发生的敌对行动。',('The agreement called for an immediate end to hostilities.','协议要求立即停止敌对行动。'),('The village was evacuated before hostilities began.','战事开始前，村民已经撤离。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/hostilities','https://www.etymonline.com/word/hostility']),
E('hostilely','英 /ˈhɒstaɪli/；美 /ˈhɑːstəli/','带敌意地；敌对地','说话、看人或回应时，把排斥和对抗的态度露出来。','hostile + -ly；读音随 hostile 的英美常见变体变化。',HOSTILE+[['英语 hostile + -ly → hostilely','敌对的 → 带敌意地']],'常配 react、respond、look 等动作。它较书面，口语也会说 in a hostile way。不能见 -ly 就以为它一定表示声音很大；冷冷的一眼也可能 hostile。','respond hostilely；react hostilely；look at someone hostilely。','angrily 是生气地；hostilely 更突出把对方当作对手的态度。',('He stared hostilely at the unfamiliar visitors.','他带着敌意盯着那些陌生来客。'),('The group reacted hostilely to the proposed changes.','这个团体以强烈敌对的态度回应拟议的变更。'),sources=['https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/hostilely','https://www.etymonline.com/word/hostile']),
